fix(P0): eliminate attention sort cap with 2-phase query

Phase 1: lightweight query fetches ALL matching samples with only
id, status, updatedAt, and work item statuses (minimal memory).
Computes attention rank in memory, sorts, slices for the page,
extracts just the IDs.

Phase 2: fetches full data (with all includes) for only
the page's IDs, then re-orders to match the ranked sort.

This eliminates the 10K cap that caused wrong/empty pages when
total samples exceeded the cap while pagination reported the
real DB count.
